 [17592186411675 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186411657 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186411675 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186411663 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186411675 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045494 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186411675 #edb/ref 1077 "field-3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186411675 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186411645 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186411675 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "a96a19a5-4d57-5c70-b981-f077301f5ca5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186411676 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186411621 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186411676 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186411631 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186411676 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186411634 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186411676 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186411642 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186411676 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186411655 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186411676 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045494 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186411676 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186411676 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186411634 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186411676 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "cbaddc60-4ab1-53ea-a39d-217315412f69" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186411677 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186411668 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186411677 #edb/ref 1069 "q-212923" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186411677 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186411677 #edb/ref 1071 "Given the relation $R$ on $N$ defined by\n\n$$\nx\\,R\\,y\\,⇔\\,x>y,\n$$\n\nwhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $6\\,R\\,8$\n\nII. $7\\,R\\,2$\n\nIII. $9\\,\\cancel{\\,R\\,}\\,1$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186411677 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "579647d8-78b0-511b-8a94-882ec6fc1b22" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186411677 #edb/ref 1074 "A relation $R$ on a set $A$ is a subset of the Cartesian product $A\\times A={A}^{2}.$\n\n$$\nR⊆A\\times A\n$$\n\nWe also have the following notations:\n\n- $x\\,R\\,y$ if and only if $(x,y)\\in R$\n\n- $x\\,\\cancel{\\,R\\,}\\,y$ if and only if $(x,y)\\notin R$\n\nIn this case, we have $x\\,R\\,y$ if and only if $x>y.$ For this relation, note that\n\n- the symbols $R$ and $>$ are interchangeable, and\n\n- the symbols $\\cancel{\\,R\\,}$ and $≯$ (or, equivalently, $\\cancel{\\,R\\,}$ and $\\le $) are also interchangeable.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn:\n\n- Statement I is false. Replacing $R$ with the symbol $>,$ we have $6>8,$ which is false.\n\n- Statement II is true. Replacing $R$ with the symbol $>,$ we have $7>2,$ which is true.\n\n- Statement III is false. Replacing $\\cancel{\\,R\\,}$ with the symbol $\\le ,$ we have $9\\le 1,$ which is false.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186411678 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186411670 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186411678 #edb/ref 1069 "q-212926" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186411678 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186411678 #edb/ref 1071 "Given the relation $R$ on $Z$ defined by\n\n$$\nx\\,R\\,y\\,⇔\\,x∣y,\n$$\n\nwhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $6\\,R\\,3$\n\nII. $5\\,R\\,8$\n\nIII. $7\\,\\cancel{\\,R\\,}\\,9$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186411678 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a8c98d98-74bc-5116-9f06-75c38fdcf981" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186411678 #edb/ref 1074 "A relation $R$ on a set $A$ is a subset of the Cartesian product $A\\times A={A}^{2}.$\n\n$$\nR⊆A\\times A\n$$\n\nWe also have the following notations:\n\n- $x\\,R\\,y$ if and only if $(x,y)\\in R$\n\n- $x\\,\\cancel{\\,R\\,}\\,y$ if and only if $(x,y)\\notin R$\n\nIn this case, we have $x\\,R\\,y$ if and only if $x∣y.$ For this relation, note that\n\n- the symbols $R$ and $∣$ are interchangeable, and\n\n- the symbols $\\cancel{\\,R\\,}$ and $∤$ are also interchangeable.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn:\n\n- Statement I is false. Replacing $R$ with the symbol $∣,$ we have $6∣3,$ which is false.\n\n- Statement II is false. Replacing $R$ with the symbol $∣,$ we have $5∣8,$ which is false.\n\n- Statement III is true. Replacing $\\cancel{\\,R\\,}$ with the symbol $∤,$ we have $7∤9,$ which is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186411679 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186411673 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186411679 #edb/ref 1069 "q-212983" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186411679 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186411679 #edb/ref 1071 "Given the relation $R$ on $Z$ defined by\n\n$$\nx\\,R\\,y\\,⇔\\,x≡y+4\\,(\\text{mod}\\,6),\n$$\n\nwhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $0\\,R\\,2$\n\nII. $1\\,R\\,9$\n\nIII. $4\\,\\cancel{\\,R\\,}\\,13$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186411679 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b5b2a52b-fd77-5422-b1dc-3a9ca690060e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186411679 #edb/ref 1074 "A relation $R$ on a set $A$ is a subset of the Cartesian product $A\\times A={A}^{2}.$\n\n$$\nR⊆A\\times A\n$$\n\nWe also have the following notations:\n\n- $x\\,R\\,y$ if and only if $(x,y)\\in R$\n\n- $x\\,\\cancel{\\,R\\,}\\,y$ if and only if $(x,y)\\notin R$\n\nIn this case, we have $x\\,R\\,y$ if and only if $x≡y+4\\,(\\text{mod}\\,6),$ or equivalently, $x\\,R\\,y$ if and only if $6∣(x-y-4).$ \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn:\n\n- Statement I is true. In this case, we have $6∣(0-2-4),$ which is true.\n\n- Statement II is true. In this case, we have $6∣(1-9-4),$ which is true.\n\n- Statement III is true. In this case, we have $6∤(4-13-4),$ which is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186411680 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186411669 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186411680 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186411671 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186411680 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186411676 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186411680 #edb/ref 1069 "q-218358" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186411680 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186411680 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $A=Z,$ and consider the relation $R$ on $A$ such that $x\\,R\\,y$ if and only if $3\\,|\\,(x+y).$ Express $R$ using set-builder notation.\n\n$$\nR={{{field-1}}\\in {{field-2}}\\,:\\,{{field-3}}}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186411680 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e2674a53-8856-5a0e-8ea3-7bef241518ca" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186411680 #edb/ref 1074 "A relation $R$ on a set $A$ is a subset of the Cartesian product $A\\times A={A}^{2}.$\n\n$$\nR⊆A\\times A\n$$\n\nFor a relation $R$ on a set $A,$ we also have the following notations:\n\n- $a\\,R\\,b$ if and only if $(a,b)\\in R$\n\n- $a\\,\\cancel{\\,R\\,}\\,b$ if and only if $(a,b)\\notin R$\n\nIn this case, $R$ is the set of ordered pairs $(x,y)\\in Z\\times Z={Z}^{2}$ such that $3\\,|\\,(x+y).$\n\nTherefore, we can write out $R$ in set-builder notation as follows:\n\n$$\nR={(x,y)\\in {Z}^{2}\\,:\\,3\\,|\\,(x+y)}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
